WEBVTT

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:14.450
<u>Alliance Navy 10th Fleet Flagship
</u>Gesir Bogdo

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:17.950
<u>10th Fleet Commander
</u>Vice Admiral Ulanhu

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:20.030
<b>Legend of the Galactic Heroes</b>

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:24.490
<u>Alliance Navy 8th Fleet Flagship
</u>Jagannath

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:26.490
All the nobles have fled.

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:29.350
Only the ruling-class citizens remain.

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:34.280
The enemy is being cautious 
after losing Iserlohn.

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:34.670
<u>8th Fleet Commander
</u>Vice Admiral Appleton

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:37.120
We are a liberating army.

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:40.960
You don't have to suffer under the 
oppression of tyranny any longer.

00:02:41.350 --> 00:02:44.840
The Free Planet Alliance is 
glad to welcome all of you.

00:02:45.430 --> 00:02:49.600
<u>Alliance Navy 12th Fleet Flagship
</u>Cernunnos

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:49.570
Word is that the citizens are 
accepting us without resistance.

00:02:50.090 --> 00:02:52.420
I never dreamed the occupation 
would be this easy.

00:02:52.820 --> 00:02:54.780
Is it the same for the other fleets?

00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:58.240
<u>12th Fleet Commander
</u>Vice Admiral Borodin

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:57.530
It seems so... ah, but...

00:02:58.450 --> 00:03:01.630
You will be given complete political 
authority over yourselves

00:03:01.630 --> 00:03:05.440
and begin your new lives as 
citizens of a free city.

00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:10.470
Excuse me... but before you give 
us this political authority,

00:03:10.470 --> 00:03:12.860
could you just give us some bread and milk?

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:16.830
O-Of course. We'll arrange it right away.

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:20.940
We have no food. I don't even 
have milk for my baby.

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:23.300
Please, just give us something, 
anything, to eat.

00:03:28.490 --> 00:03:29.230
Admiral.

00:03:30.490 --> 00:03:32.200
Message from the ground force.

00:03:32.570 --> 00:03:33.620
What is it?

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:38.790
They've asked us to send food to 
distribute among the citizens.

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:41.530
All right. Take care of it at once.

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:42.200
Yes, sir.

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:51.120
<b>Episode 11</b>

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:51.120
<b>The Verge of Death (Part 1)</b>

00:03:51.770 --> 00:03:54.580
Could you read that report 
for me one more time?

00:03:55.490 --> 00:03:58.790
"To permanently save the 
locals from starvation

00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:02.590
will require 180 days' worth of 
food for fifty million people,

00:04:02.590 --> 00:04:04.750
forty artificial protein production plants,

00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:06.410
and sixty hydroponics plants.

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:08.970
These numbers are expected to rise

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:12.190
as the liberated territory 
further expands."

00:04:12.670 --> 00:04:15.210
That's ten million tons of grain alone.

00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:18.070
That would take fifty cargo ships 
in the 200,000-ton class...

00:04:18.890 --> 00:04:24.160
Who could come up with a supply plan to feed 
twice as many people as our entire navy?

00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:27.140
Even if we emptied every 
warehouse in Iserlohn—

00:04:27.140 --> 00:04:28.270
It wouldn't be enough.

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:31.110
We'd run out in the blink of an eye.

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:37.230
Forgive me for interrupting.

00:04:38.390 --> 00:04:40.360
Ah, you're here.

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:42.990
I heard you had something 
you wanted to discuss.

00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:44.980
Keep it short, if you would.

00:04:44.980 --> 00:04:47.420
I'll be brief, then.

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:51.470
Your Excellency, our navy is 
facing a serious crisis.

00:04:51.890 --> 00:04:54.060
What brought this on?

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:57.720
You are aware of the request 
from the front line, I assume?

00:04:57.720 --> 00:04:59.270
I've heard, of course.

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:01.960
It is certainly an excessive request,

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:04.740
but our occupation policy 
leaves us no other choice.

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:08.060
We don't have that much 
food in all of Iserlohn.

00:05:08.060 --> 00:05:10.700
So forward the request to our home country.

00:05:11.050 --> 00:05:13.010
The bureaucrats may complain,

00:05:13.010 --> 00:05:16.080
but there's no way our politicians 
won't send the food.

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:18.980
Yes, I'm sure they would send it.

00:05:18.980 --> 00:05:21.910
But how long could they keep it up?

00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:27.460
The enemy's plan is to place a 
massive strain on our supplies.

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:29.640
Which means without question, our supply—

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:30.010
Without question,

00:05:30.010 --> 00:05:32.080
they will attack our supply corps

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:34.850
in an attempt to sever our supply line.

00:05:35.410 --> 00:05:38.560
Is that what you believe, 
Rear Admiral Caselnes?

00:05:39.210 --> 00:05:40.570
Precisely.

00:05:42.050 --> 00:05:45.220
The entire region of space between 
Iserlohn and the front line

00:05:45.220 --> 00:05:47.270
is under our control.

00:05:47.730 --> 00:05:49.770
We have nothing to worry about.

00:05:50.260 --> 00:05:54.370
Rear Admiral, we're fighting 
this war for the greater good.

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:57.740
What victory can be gained 
without taking risks?

00:05:57.740 --> 00:05:59.710
That is not what I came here to discuss!

00:06:00.030 --> 00:06:04.660
Enough. I don't have time to 
cater to your cowardice.

00:06:04.660 --> 00:06:05.670
Leave.

00:06:06.920 --> 00:06:09.550
I have said what needed to be said.

00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:11.430
I will take my leave.

00:06:12.050 --> 00:06:14.970
<i>Yang, please come back alive.</i>

00:06:15.330 --> 00:06:18.090
<i>This battle is too idiotic to die for.</i>

00:06:18.990 --> 00:06:22.180
<i>After receiving the massive request 
for supplies from the front line,</i>

00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:25.100
<i>the High Council was thrown into chaos.</i>

00:06:25.700 --> 00:06:29.100
<i>Those who favored continuing the war, 
represented by Councilor Windsor,</i>

00:06:29.510 --> 00:06:32.480
<i>were locked in a fierce verbal 
battle with Councilor Lebello,</i>

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:34.260
<i>who wished to withdraw the troops.</i>

00:06:34.810 --> 00:06:35.870
<i>However...</i>

00:06:36.220 --> 00:06:38.610
I will now announce the 
results of the vote.

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:42.540
Four in favor, five opposed, 
with two abstaining.

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:44.140
With a majority opposed,

00:06:44.140 --> 00:06:48.080
the motion to withdraw from the 
current operation is rejected.

00:06:48.690 --> 00:06:53.640
<i>As a result, it was decided that the 
invasion into the Empire would continue.</i>

00:06:56.070 --> 00:06:58.410
<i>With the High Council's decision made,</i>

00:06:58.410 --> 00:07:02.320
<i>supply ships departed for 
Iserlohn from Heinessen.</i>

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:05.310
<i>However, it was already too late.</i>

00:07:05.310 --> 00:07:10.610
<i>Supplies at the front line 
were already running dry.</i>

00:07:13.070 --> 00:07:14.400
Ridiculous!

00:07:15.060 --> 00:07:18.370
You expect us to acquire the 
supplies we need locally?!

00:07:18.710 --> 00:07:22.330
Are you telling us to go 
out and start looting?

00:07:22.690 --> 00:07:26.290
How are we supposed to 
loot what isn't there?

00:07:26.790 --> 00:07:30.760
A failed supply plan is the 
first step toward defeat.

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:35.250
Whatever happened to all that 
big talk from command?

00:07:36.470 --> 00:07:40.980
<u>Alliance Navy 13th Fleet Flagship
</u>Hyperion

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:39.720
They all seem rather angry.

00:07:39.720 --> 00:07:41.180
Of course they are.

00:07:41.180 --> 00:07:44.070
Our own fleet is running low on food,

00:07:44.070 --> 00:07:47.140
but we can't let all those 
people starve now.

00:07:47.510 --> 00:07:50.350
If the Imperial Navy were 
to bring them food,

00:07:50.350 --> 00:07:54.480
everyone in the Empire would be 
singing their kaiser's praises.

00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:59.050
Why must we starve ourselves 
to feed all those people?

00:07:59.050 --> 00:08:00.450
Patrichev.

00:08:03.240 --> 00:08:06.430
So that we don't become Rudolf, that's why.

00:08:07.180 --> 00:08:10.980
Sub-lieutenant, call Vice Admiral 
Ulanhu at once, please.

00:08:10.980 --> 00:08:12.920
Right away, Admiral.

00:08:15.160 --> 00:08:18.460
<i>Ah, Yang Wen-li. I don't 
often hear from you.</i>

00:08:18.460 --> 00:08:22.130
Vice Admiral Ulanhu, 
I'm glad to see you're well.

00:08:22.130 --> 00:08:26.850
<i>Like hell I am. I'm dealing 
with the same problem as you.</i>

00:08:28.040 --> 00:08:31.560
Anyway, how are our supply 
reserves looking?

00:08:31.560 --> 00:08:34.420
<i>We have enough to last another week.</i>

00:08:34.420 --> 00:08:36.490
<i>If we don't receive more by then,</i>

00:08:36.490 --> 00:08:39.030
<i>we may have no choice
but to requisition...</i>

00:08:39.030 --> 00:08:40.130
<i>No...</i>

00:08:40.130 --> 00:08:42.500
<i>It's no use mincing words.</i>

00:08:42.840 --> 00:08:45.700
<i>We'll have to loot it from 
the occupied territory.</i>

00:08:46.320 --> 00:08:48.900
<i>Some "liberating army" we are.</i>

00:08:51.620 --> 00:08:55.100
I have an idea concerning 
that matter, if I may...

00:08:57.870 --> 00:08:59.240
<i>Retreat?!</i>

00:08:59.240 --> 00:09:01.550
<i>Before we even exchange the first fire?</i>

00:09:01.980 --> 00:09:04.240
Yes, while we still have reserves.

00:09:04.240 --> 00:09:07.070
The enemy is waiting for 
us to starve as a result

00:09:07.070 --> 00:09:09.050
of the strain on our supplies.

00:09:09.390 --> 00:09:13.070
<i>Are you saying they're waiting for the 
right moment to shift to the offensive?</i>

00:09:13.490 --> 00:09:16.220
With an all-out attack, most likely.

00:09:16.220 --> 00:09:18.230
They have the locational advantage,

00:09:18.230 --> 00:09:20.210
and their supply line will be short.

00:09:20.530 --> 00:09:22.540
We are right in the heart of the enemy.

00:09:22.810 --> 00:09:25.610
<i>Hmm... But if we retreat carelessly,</i>

00:09:25.610 --> 00:09:28.810
<i>wouldn't it just invite 
the enemy to attack?</i>

00:09:29.220 --> 00:09:31.880
<i>We'd be stirring up a hornet's nest.</i>

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:34.860
We would have to be fully 
prepared to counterattack.

00:09:34.860 --> 00:09:36.510
That is essential.

00:09:37.080 --> 00:09:40.980
We could manage that right now, 
but it'll be too late once our men starve.

00:09:41.430 --> 00:09:44.480
We have no choice but to 
make an orderly retreat.

00:09:46.580 --> 00:09:47.930
<i>Go on.</i>

00:09:49.190 --> 00:09:51.830
If the enemy interprets our withdrawal

00:09:51.830 --> 00:09:54.900
as a total rout, that will 
work out just fine.

00:09:55.510 --> 00:09:59.110
We'll have several possible ways 
to fight back if they pursue us.

00:09:59.530 --> 00:10:03.940
If they think it's too soon, or that 
it's a trap, that suits us as well.

00:10:04.470 --> 00:10:06.890
We may be able to withdraw unscathed.

00:10:07.410 --> 00:10:09.660
The odds are not high,

00:10:09.660 --> 00:10:12.810
but with each passing day, they fall lower.

00:10:13.890 --> 00:10:16.980
The best route we could take

00:10:16.980 --> 00:10:19.810
would be to retreat as quickly as possible.

00:10:22.390 --> 00:10:26.020
<i>I understand. I'm sure you're right.</i>

00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:28.600
<i>I will have our men prepare to withdraw.</i>

00:10:29.030 --> 00:10:30.050
I'm glad.

00:10:30.050 --> 00:10:34.050
<i>But how do we tell command and all 
the other fleets about this?</i>

00:10:34.510 --> 00:10:37.270
I intend to ask Admiral 
Bewcock to inform them.

00:10:37.720 --> 00:10:40.570
I think having him talk to all of them

00:10:40.970 --> 00:10:44.200
would be more effective 
than doing it myself.

00:10:45.500 --> 00:10:49.060
<i>Then I suppose we'd both better move quickly.</i>

00:10:51.730 --> 00:10:54.130
I agree with your proposal.

00:10:54.580 --> 00:10:56.910
I have no objections, either.

00:10:56.910 --> 00:10:59.100
I think it's an excellent decision.

00:10:59.100 --> 00:11:00.080
Please.

00:11:00.590 --> 00:11:02.450
Flattery will get you nowhere.

00:11:03.340 --> 00:11:04.470
Urgent report!

00:11:04.470 --> 00:11:07.310
A revolt has broken out in the territory 
occupied by the 8th Fleet!

00:11:07.310 --> 00:11:09.070
It's a massive uprising!

00:11:13.730 --> 00:11:16.400
Hey! There's food over here!

00:11:16.760 --> 00:11:18.640
Do you know how to use a gun?

00:11:18.640 --> 00:11:19.350
Yeah!

00:11:19.350 --> 00:11:22.370
Put the gun down! Refuse and I'll shoot!

00:11:22.370 --> 00:11:23.990
He's next!

00:11:26.070 --> 00:11:28.050
How did this happen?!

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:51.900
What a tragedy this turned out to be.

00:11:52.410 --> 00:11:56.810
There's no way we can build mutual 
trust with the people now.

00:11:57.200 --> 00:11:58.170
Yeah...

00:11:58.700 --> 00:12:03.890
The enemy has succeeded in getting 
between us and the people of the Empire.

00:12:05.850 --> 00:12:08.390
<i>Even if I knew it would bring us victory,</i>

00:12:10.420 --> 00:12:13.350
<i>I could never bring myself 
to be this thorough.</i>

00:12:15.620 --> 00:12:19.420
<i>Well done indeed, Count Lohengramm.</i>

00:12:22.140 --> 00:12:24.190
Put me through to Admiral Bewcock.

00:12:24.570 --> 00:12:25.470
Yes, sir.

00:12:26.200 --> 00:12:29.140
<i>Bewcock accepted Yang's 
proposal to withdraw</i>

00:12:26.470 --> 00:12:32.690
<u>Alliance Navy  5th Fleet Flagship
</u>Rio Grande

00:12:29.140 --> 00:12:31.520
<i>and pushed for a retreat to Iserlohn.</i>

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:36.380
<i>To do so, he requested correspondence 
with Supreme Commander Lobos.</i>

00:12:37.390 --> 00:12:39.620
Where is the supreme commander?

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:43.380
<i>Admiral Bewcock, how can I help you?</i>

00:12:45.100 --> 00:12:47.230
I didn't say I wanted to see you.

00:12:47.620 --> 00:12:49.780
Don't butt in where you 
haven't been called.

00:12:49.780 --> 00:12:55.200
<i>All communications with Fleet Admiral 
Lobos will be conducted through me.</i>

00:12:56.530 --> 00:12:58.420
I have no need to speak to you.

00:12:58.420 --> 00:13:01.410
<i>Then I cannot relay your message to him.</i>

00:13:01.410 --> 00:13:02.690
What?

00:13:02.690 --> 00:13:06.960
<i>No matter how high your rank, you are 
required to comply with regulations.</i>

00:13:06.960 --> 00:13:08.890
<i>Shall I end this transmission?</i>

00:13:11.420 --> 00:13:15.150
All the commanders of the fleets at 
the front line wish to retreat.

00:13:15.150 --> 00:13:18.850
I want to request the supreme commander's 
understanding on this matter.

00:13:19.250 --> 00:13:20.950
<i>Retreat, you say?</i>

00:13:20.950 --> 00:13:22.780
<i>Admiral Yang is one thing,</i>

00:13:22.780 --> 00:13:25.220
<i>but to hear the brave Admiral Bewcock</i>

00:13:25.220 --> 00:13:28.810
<i>calling for a retreat without 
even fighting is a surprise.</i>

00:13:29.370 --> 00:13:31.480
Spare me the snide comments.

00:13:31.810 --> 00:13:36.790
This wouldn't have happened if you people 
hadn't proposed such a reckless operation.

00:13:36.790 --> 00:13:39.600
Why don't you try assuming 
a little responsibility?

00:13:39.600 --> 00:13:42.100
<i>If it were me, I would not retreat.</i>

00:13:42.470 --> 00:13:45.950
<i>This is our chance to strike down the 
entire Imperial Navy in one attack.</i>

00:13:45.950 --> 00:13:48.260
<i>What are you so afraid of?</i>

00:13:50.270 --> 00:13:53.360
Fine. Then I'll trade you places.

00:13:53.730 --> 00:13:56.320
I'm returning to Iserlohn.

00:13:56.320 --> 00:13:59.040
You can come to the front 
line to take my place.

00:13:59.040 --> 00:14:01.560
<i>Please don't ask for what 
you know is impossible.</i>

00:14:03.120 --> 00:14:05.960
You're the one proposing the impossible.

00:14:06.490 --> 00:14:10.400
And without taking a step from 
that safe haven you're in.

00:14:10.400 --> 00:14:14.440
<i>Are you... insulting me?</i>

00:14:14.910 --> 00:14:17.510
I'm just sick of hearing your big talk.

00:14:18.300 --> 00:14:21.900
If you want to demonstrate your talents,

00:14:21.900 --> 00:14:24.220
do it through actual 
achievements, not talk!

00:14:24.850 --> 00:14:29.670
Why don't you get out here 
yourself and find out

00:14:30.070 --> 00:14:32.670
whether you're capable of 
giving orders to others?!

00:14:41.060 --> 00:14:42.840
<i>Hey! We've got trouble!</i>

00:14:42.840 --> 00:14:45.080
<i>Commodore! Commodore Falk!</i>

00:14:45.080 --> 00:14:47.380
What the hell just happened?

00:14:49.330 --> 00:14:50.940
<i>Admiral Bewcock.</i>

00:14:52.030 --> 00:14:54.670
Well, this is quite an honor, Chief of Staff.

00:14:55.190 --> 00:14:58.130
<i>I'm sorry you had to see 
that shameful display.</i>

00:14:58.660 --> 00:15:00.330
What happened to him?

00:15:00.330 --> 00:15:03.400
<i>Well, according to our physician,</i>

00:15:03.400 --> 00:15:07.800
<i>he was so overstimulated by his own 
intense frustration that he had a seizure.</i>

00:15:08.340 --> 00:15:10.730
<i>Since it's caused by a mental condition,</i>

00:15:10.730 --> 00:15:12.760
<i>if that cause is not eliminated,</i>

00:15:12.760 --> 00:15:16.540
<i>he is likely to have more episodes 
like this in the future.</i>

00:15:16.950 --> 00:15:19.780
<i>What should we do, then?</i>

00:15:20.140 --> 00:15:23.360
<i>Don't defy him, don't make 
him feel frustrated,</i>

00:15:23.360 --> 00:15:27.280
<i>and make sure everything goes 
his way, the physician said.</i>

00:15:29.570 --> 00:15:31.650
Are you being serious?

00:15:32.000 --> 00:15:36.200
<i>As far as treating him goes, 
there is one natural course of action.</i>

00:15:36.820 --> 00:15:39.620
That's obvious. We should get rid of him.

00:15:40.300 --> 00:15:43.620
If they knew a man with the 
mentality of a child was working

00:15:43.620 --> 00:15:46.750
as the tactician for a fleet 
of thirty million men,

00:15:46.750 --> 00:15:49.760
the Imperial Army would have a field day.

00:15:50.590 --> 00:15:54.030
So, what do you say about 
the proposal to retreat?

00:15:54.650 --> 00:16:00.310
The men at the front line are in no 
condition to fight, mentally or physically.

00:16:00.650 --> 00:16:02.500
<i>Please wait for a bit.</i>

00:16:02.870 --> 00:16:06.190
<i>That would require the supreme 
commander's approval.</i>

00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:09.530
<i>Understand that I can't give 
you an immediate answer.</i>

00:16:09.890 --> 00:16:11.980
This is an urgent matter!

00:16:11.980 --> 00:16:13.960
I realize I'm being impolite,

00:16:13.960 --> 00:16:18.990
but can't you arrange an audience 
with the supreme commander for me?

00:16:20.650 --> 00:16:25.090
<i>The supreme commander is currently resting.</i>

00:16:25.090 --> 00:16:28.300
Huh? What did you just say?

00:16:28.670 --> 00:16:32.820
<i>The supreme commander is currently resting.</i>

00:16:33.380 --> 00:16:36.900
<i>He has given orders not to wake 
him unless the enemy attacks.</i>

00:16:37.210 --> 00:16:40.800
<i>I will relay your request 
to him once he wakes up.</i>

00:16:40.800 --> 00:16:43.090
<i>Please wait until then.</i>

00:16:45.250 --> 00:16:48.260
Fine. I get it.

00:16:48.680 --> 00:16:51.100
Then, as the front-line commander,

00:16:51.100 --> 00:16:54.640
I am required to fulfill my obligation 
to the lives of my subordinates.

00:16:55.230 --> 00:16:57.280
I apologize for taking up your time.

00:16:57.280 --> 00:17:01.340
When the supreme commander wakes up,

00:17:01.340 --> 00:17:04.580
please tell him that Bewcock 
hopes he had pleasant dreams.

00:17:05.290 --> 00:17:06.210
Signing off.

00:17:06.720 --> 00:17:07.440
<i>Admir—</i>

00:17:08.290 --> 00:17:11.300
<u></u>Galactic Empire Capital Planet Odin

00:17:12.100 --> 00:17:15.940
A supply fleet will be sent to 
the front line from Iserlohn.

00:17:16.840 --> 00:17:18.360
That's the enemy's lifeline.

00:17:18.760 --> 00:17:22.740
Use all the troops I've 
given you to strike.

00:17:23.590 --> 00:17:26.540
I'll leave it up to your talent 
to work out the details.

00:17:27.020 --> 00:17:28.300
Understood.

00:17:29.800 --> 00:17:30.790
I'll be going.

00:17:31.980 --> 00:17:32.980
Wait.

00:17:36.020 --> 00:17:38.740
You don't seem to agree with this plan.

00:17:39.840 --> 00:17:42.580
No, that's not true.

00:17:43.760 --> 00:17:47.200
I can tell what you're thinking.

00:17:50.870 --> 00:17:54.250
I am aware that this plan has been 
devised to assure our victory.

00:17:55.100 --> 00:17:55.590
But—

00:17:55.590 --> 00:17:58.400
You don't want a strategy that 
puts a burden on the people?

00:18:00.400 --> 00:18:03.360
We're doing it to win, Kircheis.

00:18:07.330 --> 00:18:10.480
Yes. I know.

00:18:27.040 --> 00:18:32.420
While Admiral Kircheis wipes out 
the rebel force's supply fleet,

00:18:32.420 --> 00:18:34.750
our navy will shift to a major offensive.

00:18:35.480 --> 00:18:37.650
In accordance with the existing plan,

00:18:37.650 --> 00:18:41.120
our goal will be to swiftly 
mop up all the rebels.

00:18:41.580 --> 00:18:43.250
That is all I have to say.

00:18:47.600 --> 00:18:51.220
Our navy will take back 
the captured territory,

00:18:51.220 --> 00:18:53.270
while delivering food to the people.

00:18:54.150 --> 00:18:57.270
Even if it was to counter 
the rebels' invasion,

00:18:57.270 --> 00:19:01.150
it was not my wish to force 
the people into poverty.

00:19:02.060 --> 00:19:03.830
We must win this battle

00:19:03.830 --> 00:19:08.830
and prove that we are the ones 
worthy to rule the land.

00:19:09.770 --> 00:19:14.300
Do not let those arrogant 
insurgents return home alive.

00:19:15.110 --> 00:19:16.410
Mittermeyer.

00:19:16.410 --> 00:19:17.210
Sir!

00:19:17.810 --> 00:19:19.210
Reuenthal.

00:19:19.210 --> 00:19:19.930
Sir!

00:19:20.460 --> 00:19:21.880
Bittenfeld.

00:19:21.880 --> 00:19:22.690
Sir!

00:19:23.210 --> 00:19:24.290
Kempff.

00:19:24.290 --> 00:19:25.050
Sir!

00:19:25.730 --> 00:19:26.920
Mecklinger.

00:19:26.920 --> 00:19:27.850
Sir!

00:19:28.220 --> 00:19:29.360
Wahlen.

00:19:29.360 --> 00:19:30.300
Sir!

00:19:30.630 --> 00:19:31.740
Lutz.

00:19:31.740 --> 00:19:32.510
Sir!

00:19:34.400 --> 00:19:36.310
I expect the best from all of you.

00:19:36.700 --> 00:19:37.640
Yes, sir!

00:19:37.980 --> 00:19:42.200
May the great god Odin bestow 
his favor upon you.

00:19:43.610 --> 00:19:44.910
Prosit!

00:19:45.950 --> 00:19:47.400
Prosit!

00:19:48.290 --> 00:19:49.780
Prosit!

00:20:10.830 --> 00:20:12.310
Notice to the engine department.

00:20:12.310 --> 00:20:14.790
Transitioning to phase 3 of 
preparation for departure.

00:20:14.790 --> 00:20:18.990
Traffic control report. 
No threats observed in the area.

00:20:18.990 --> 00:20:23.440
Damage control personnel, shift observation 
of major sectors to alert level 2.

00:20:23.440 --> 00:20:27.470
No warning signals or shutdown 
notices given for our departure.

00:20:27.470 --> 00:20:30.060
Data link with control center is ongoing.

00:20:30.570 --> 00:20:32.820
Imperial transport authority
departure checklist

00:20:32.820 --> 00:20:37.330
for reactor and reactor control
systems complete.

00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:40.320
Our fleet's departure signal 
has received the response,

00:20:40.320 --> 00:20:43.770
"Permission granted. Comply with 
regulation departure speed."

00:20:49.390 --> 00:20:51.880
Brünhild is in in-port pilot mode,

00:20:51.880 --> 00:20:53.630
advancing at departure speed.

00:24:50.010 --> 00:25:00.010
<b>Episode 12</b>

00:24:50.010 --> 00:25:00.010
<b>The Verge of Death (Part 2)</b>

00:24:50.490 --> 00:24:55.040
<i>Next time on </i>Legend of 
 the Galactic Heroes - Die Neue These<i>,</i>

00:24:55.040 --> 00:24:59.490
